data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` into a `Span` of native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5, when `nint` and `nuint` were introduced as first-class types (aliases for `IntPtr` / `UIntPtr`). On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes; on a 32-bit runtime they'd be 4 bytes.
